  "interpretation": [
    "Both independent epochs select map-frame wall x centers 3.05, 2.95, 3.05 m across snapshots 01–03. The alternating side of the wall-aligned 0.1 m cell boundary is repeatable; this is consistent with grid-side quantization but does not identify the mapping cause.",
    "All 72 #296 snapshot-01 >0.10 m wall SDF outliers inverse-transform to the same 2.95 m map-frame x center. The run alignment shifts their world x by a median −54.5 mm (P05/P95 −61.2/−50.4 mm), producing nearest-SDF distances with median 104.5 mm and P95 111.2 mm. One-cell quantization combined with the evaluation alignment is therefore a strong candidate explanation for this threshold crossing.",
    "At #296 snapshot 01, the same-y/z analytic front face for 30 of those 72 samples projects inside the source-time image rectangle; 16 voxel centers themselves project inside. All 72 centers project inside at least one logged pose after the first motion command, but snapshots do not preserve per-voxel observation times."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The wall ROI is frustum-only; analytic sample projection does not ray-cast box/cylinder occlusion or model missing/invalid depth returns.",
    "A voxel snapshot has no per-voxel observation timestamps. Historic visibility checks only show that a logged VINS pose could project the point into the image after the first recorded motion command.",
    "The single rigid alignment is fitted to the full VINS/truth trajectory. Its small rotation can shift distant wall samples by several centimetres; this is a diagnostic coordinate transform, not online map correction.",
    "The 0.10 m nearest-SDF distance is exploratory and equals one configured voxel width; no acceptance threshold or formal visible ROI is frozen.",
    "The ROI is a pinhole frustum bound, not an occlusion-aware visible surface or a depth-return coverage count; it does not prove completeness or exclude duplicated surfaces.",
    "The 0.10 m SDF cutoff equals one voxel width and is diagnostic only. A small full-run alignment rotation is poorly constrained by this short trajectory and is not an independent map calibration."
  ],
